    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nHello! I discovered mini.hues and mini.base16 plugins to create custom colorschemes. One thing that I figured out, is that in mini.base16 \"FloatTitle\" is linked to the \"Title\" hl group, so it looks strange (to my liking of course). In mini.hues that is not the same, so I begun questioning, is it intentional or not? Here is examples:\n\n## mini.hues (randomhue)\n\n<img width=\"417\" height=\"238\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e21e885-5320-45d2-8d3d-4f3ef44fd616\" />\n\nAnd FloatTitle is not a link:\n\n```lua\n{\n  bg = 1774112,\n  bold = true,\n  cterm = {\n    bold = true\n  },\n  fg = 14203373\n}\n```\n\n## mini.base16 (minicyan)\n\n<img width=\"422\" height=\"217\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70f78633-9bf9-4b75-8938-d8724fbb698f\" />\n\nAnd FloatTitle is a link:\n\n```lua\n{\n  link = \"Title\"\n}\n```\n\nI know that you can override these, but I think it is strange to see autogeneration with less data passed in (hues) look more consistent than autogeneration with more data (base16).\n",
