    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> One thing that I figured out, is that in mini.base16 \"FloatTitle\" is linked to the \"Title\" hl group, so it looks strange (to my liking of course). In mini.hues that is not the same, so I begun questioning, is it intentional or not?\n\nYes, this intentional. The goal of 'mini.base16' is to stick to the [original Vim base16](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16-vim) theme. As that doesn't have `FloatTitle` highlight group defined (it is Neovim specific group, Vim doesn't have one), the default link is used. Which makes `FloatTitle` link to `Title` (you can see that inside `nvim --clean` by executing `:hi FloatTitle`).\n\nI personally also don't really like the way it looks, so when designing 'mini.hues' there is an explicit `FloatTitle` definition to have the same background as the rest of the floating window.\n\nMaking explicit `FloatTitle` group definition in 'mini.base16' will mean parting ways with its initial goal. It *might* happen, but would require a larger overhaul. At the same time, it would just make it more similar to 'mini.hues', which is not great for variety.\n\nSo closing this as expected behavior.",
